---
const regimes = [
  {
    area: "foundation",
    title: "Foundation Models",
    example: "e.g., LLMs",
    information: "High",
    rules: "Complex, contextual language patterns",
    signals: "Rich text and training signals",
    solution: "Pretraining & scaling",
  },
  {
    area: "markets",
    title: "Human Digital Markets",
    example: "My research focus",
    information: "Low",
    rules: "Adaptive decisions & strategic responses",
    signals: "Policy-shaped data; missing counterfactuals",
    solution: "?",
  },
  {
    area: "games",
    title: "Closed Games",
    example: "e.g., AlphaGo Zero",
    information: "High",
    rules: "Fixed rules and explicit rewards",
    signals: "Repeatable self-play simulations",
    solution: "Simulation, search & RL",
  },
  {
    area: "physics",
    title: "Classical Physics",
    example: "e.g., Planetary Orbits",
    information: "Low",
    rules: "Stable governing laws",
    signals: "Limited real-world observations",
    solution: "Theory-driven modeling",
  },
];

const transfers = [
  {
    source: "Foundation Models → Digital Markets",
    description: "Use high-dimensional learning, language reasoning, and multimodal representations to incorporate richer information into empirical models.",
  },
  {
    source: "Classical Physics → Digital Markets",
    description: "Borrow theory-guided modeling to represent how preferences, beliefs, and incentives generate observed decisions, rather than merely fitting behavioral patterns.",
  },
  {
    source: "Closed Games → Digital Markets",
    description: "Use experiments and causal inference to identify how behavior changes under alternative policies when real-world decisions cannot be replayed.",
  },
];
---

<section class="learning-matrix shell" aria-labelledby="matrix-title">
  <header class="matrix-heading">
    <h2 id="matrix-title">The Limits of Scaling</h2>
    <p>An Empirical Learning Matrix</p>
  </header>

  <div class="matrix-grid" aria-label="Four regimes of empirical modeling by complexity of rules and effective information availability">
    <div class="information-axis">← Effective Information Availability</div>
    <div class="information-label high-information">
      <strong>High</strong>
      <span>Rich Signals &amp; Feedback</span>
    </div>
    <div class="information-label low-information">
      <strong>Low</strong>
      <span>Limited Signals &amp; Feedback</span>
    </div>

    <div class="rules-axis">
      <span class="rules-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      <span class="rules-axis-name">Complexity of Rules</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rules-label high-rules">
      <strong>High</strong>
      <span>Complex &amp; Adaptive</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rules-label low-rules">
      <strong>Low</strong>
      <span>Simple &amp; Stable</span>
    </div>

    {regimes.map((regime) => (
      <article class:list={["regime", regime.area]}>
        <header>
          <p class="mobile-information">{regime.information} Information</p>
          <h3>{regime.title}</h3>
          <p class="example">{regime.example}</p>
        </header>
        <h4>Condition</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>{regime.rules}</li>
          <li>{regime.signals}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="solution"><strong>Solution:</strong> {regime.solution}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="matrix-explanation">
    As empirical researchers, we would ideally work in the lower-left corner: known rules and rich, repeatable feedback. Digital markets rarely offer both. Behavior depends on preferences, information, and incentives, while algorithms and policies are complex and evolving. In settings such as online privacy and recommender systems, even evaluating welfare is challenging. Observed behavior alone cannot identify responses to alternative designs. More data and computation alone cannot resolve these challenges.
  </p>
  <p class="method-introduction">
    This motivates me to learn from three established modeling paradigms, adapting and combining their strengths to address the distinct challenges of digital markets:
  </p>

  <div class="method-transfers" aria-label="Ideas from established approaches applied to digital markets">
    {transfers.map((transfer) => (
      <article class="transfer">
        <h3>{transfer.source}</h3>
        <p>{transfer.description}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="research-goal">
    My goal is to understand what observed behavior alone cannot reveal—preferences, incentives, and counterfactual responses—and build that understanding directly into the design of algorithms and market mechanisms.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .learning-matrix {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-section);
  }

  .matrix-heading {
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--palette-box-border);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .matrix-heading h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-title);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .matrix-heading p {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .matrix-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--space-6) minmax(0, 0.32fr) repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    grid-template-areas:
      ". . axis axis"
      ". . infohigh infolow"
      "rules high foundation markets"
      "rules low games physics";
    column-gap: 0;
    row-gap: 0;
  }

  .information-axis {
    grid-area: axis;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .information-label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .information-label strong,
  .rules-label strong {
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .information-label span,
  .rules-label span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .high-information { grid-area: infohigh; }
  .low-information { grid-area: infolow; }

  .rules-axis {
    grid-area: rules;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-self: center;
    justify-self: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .rules-axis-name {
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .rules-label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    text-align: right;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    padding-right: var(--space-3);
  }

  .high-rules { grid-area: high; }
  .low-rules { grid-area: low; }

  .foundation { grid-area: foundation; }
  .markets { grid-area: markets; }
  .games { grid-area: games; }
  .physics { grid-area: physics; }

  .regime {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--palette-box-border);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .regime.foundation,
  .regime.markets {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .regime.foundation,
  .regime.games {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .regime.markets {
    background: var(--palette-privacy-control);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-privacy-control) 45%, var(--color-background));
  }

  .regime h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-title);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .regime .example {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .mobile-information {
    display: none;
  }

  .regime h4 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .regime ul {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .regime li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .regime .solution {
    margin: auto 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--palette-reference);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .regime .solution strong {
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .matrix-explanation {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .method-introduction {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .method-transfers {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--palette-box-border);
  }

  .research-goal {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .transfer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.5fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }

  .transfer h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-normal);
  }

  .transfer p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .matrix-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      grid-template-areas:
        "axis axis"
        "infohigh infolow"
        "rules rules"
        "high high"
        "foundation markets"
        "low low"
        "games physics";
      column-gap: 0;
      row-gap: var(--space-2);
    }

    .rules-axis {
      flex-direction: row-reverse;
      justify-self: start;
      margin-top: var(--space-3);
    }

    .rules-axis-name {
      writing-mode: horizontal-tb;
      transform: none;
    }

    .rules-label {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: flex-start;
      text-align: left;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }

    .regime {
      padding: var(--space-4);
    }

    .regime.foundation,
    .regime.games {
      border-right: 1px solid var(--palette-box-border);
    }

    .regime.foundation,
    .regime.markets {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--palette-box-border);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .matrix-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas:
        "rules"
        "high"
        "axis"
        "foundation"
        "markets"
        "low"
        "games"
        "physics";
      row-gap: var(--space-2);
    }

    .information-label {
      display: none;
    }

    .information-axis {
      margin-top: var(--space-2);
      text-align: left;
    }

    .mobile-information {
      display: block;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      color: var(--color-muted);
      line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    }

    .transfer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
